# Hardening Standards
RULE: Fail loudly for unexpected missing data. Use explicit conditionals for known missing data (trading days, delistings).
WHY: Try-except hiding business logic masks pipeline failures; defensive checks hide bugs.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/validation-patterns.md, .cursor/rules/no-empty-fallbacks.mdc
DO: Explicit `if not is_trading_day: return`; raise with clear message for unexpected missing; validate before use
NEVER: Bare except; try-except for business logic; empty fallbacks; defensive isinstance to hide type errors

RULE: All repos must use `typeCheckingMode: "strict"` in pyrightconfig.json with `reportAny`, `reportUnknown*`, and `reportMissingParameterType` all set to `"error"`. No cloud SDK exceptions — use `# pyright: ignore[reportXxx]` inline for unavoidable stub gaps.
NEVER: `typeCheckingMode: "basic"`; setting real-error rules to `"none"`; `--level warning` in basedpyright invocations
DO: `run_timeout 120 basedpyright "$SOURCE_DIR/"` — no `--level warning`; let pyrightconfig.json control severity
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md#type-checking-standards

RULE: Python must not hardcode `"/tmp"` (Bandit B108). Use `tempfile.gettempdir()` for the OS temp root; use
`tempfile.mkstemp` / `NamedTemporaryFile` / `TemporaryDirectory` for files. For `shutil.disk_usage` defaults, use
`( "/", tempfile.gettempdir(), str(Path.home()) )` and skip missing paths — see
`unified_trading_library.lifecycle.resource_profiler._default_disk_paths`.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md (Bandit B108 section)
